ture-workers/linear/14039880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5359324fa248b36458bcfecab86ea4df13f93164aa03f4664aac764d91e33922"} {"question" "q-73151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-73151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{41}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{32}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{32}$ only ${a}_{33}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{32},$ ${a}_{33},$ and ${a}_{41}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{41}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-73151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${a}_{32},$ ${a}_{33},$ and ${a}_{41}$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5359324fa248b36458bcfecab86ea4df13f93164aa03f4664aac764d91e33922"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${a}_{12}$ and ${a}_{14}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{22}$ and ${a}_{33}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{23}$ and ${a}_{33}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a42625f966b46ce68b9d3ef91530c2180d258fc6528e6c5df0f2380867f7778"} {"question" "e-6166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-6166.json" "file_sha256" "ecc46975b9672648074bca266624acd2504115680e994b7e87e5e2a1e5e7835b"} {"question" "e-6166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-6166.json" "file_sha256" "ecc46975b9672648074bca266624acd2504115680e994b7e87e5e2a1e5e7835b"} {"question" "e-4688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4688.json" "file_sha256" "46b4c31b38985034dce44d993adf9c0dc1160b33e01959ca8a4bb0af86a7fd90"} {"question" "e-4688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4688.json" "file_sha256" "46b4c31b38985034dce44d993adf9c0dc1160b33e01959ca8a4bb0af86a7fd90"} {"question" "e-4687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4687.json" "file_sha256" "203c1e0fc35513780b3743d8832441145bc026f96e039c3efbe0407b9267a626"} {"question" "e-4687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4687.json" "file_sha256" "203c1e0fc35513780b3743d8832441145bc026f96e039c3efbe0407b9267a626"} {"question" "e-4689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4689.json" "file_sha256" "1ea65c09e1096e026a31ea18f39351049ec3554e2a128d76e81e8ad5b66c9af8"} {"question" "e-4689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4689.json" "file_sha256" "1ea65c09e1096e026a31ea18f39351049ec3554e2a128d76e81e8ad5b66c9af8"}] "usage" {"q-42008" [] "e-6166" [] "q-42024" [] "e-4689" [] "q-42370" [] "e-4687" [] "e-4688" []} "basis" 1391 "retractions" [[17592186129710 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186129716 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\n\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186129709 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\n\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186129709 :question/answer-fields 17592186128048] [17592186128930 :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186128930 :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry.\n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is\n\n$$\n-1+(-4)+8=3\n$$"] [17592186128863 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186128863 :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n1. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n2. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 7 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186128862 :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186128862 :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n1. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n2. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186128864 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186128864 :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186128049 17592186128050 17592186128051 17592186128052 17592186128053 17592186128055 17592186128056 17592186128057 17592186128058 17592186128059 17592186128091 17592186128092 17592186128093 17592186128094 17592186128095] "immutable_fields" [[17592186128048 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128048 :answer-field/id] [17592186128048 :answer-field/key] [17592186128048 :answer-field/type] [17592186128054 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128054 :answer-field/id] [17592186128054 :answer-field/key] [17592186128054 :answer-field/type] [17592186128090 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128090 :answer-field/id] [17592186128090 :answer-field/key] [17592186128090 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
